From: Andrew Boyd <andrew@formkit.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drm/tiny: appletbdrm: reprobe T1 after failed resume

Propagate endpoint and display rearm failures instead of restoring a stale
framebuffer and reporting success. Mark only the failed T1 display interface
for USB core's deferred unbind/reprobe at system PM completion. Successful
resume keeps the DRM device and restores its framebuffer as before.

The private callback header allows the same production recovery sequence to
be fault-tested with synthetic USB/DRM boundaries. Hardware validation is
still required; this patch does not establish complete T1 suspend support.

